{
  "id": "V94omYjzFKbt8l7m",
  "meta": {
    "instanceId": "0e55c3b513f5a0631c17003d0888549f0d93ecb7047b38aab307f5886a32dbd4"
  },
  "name": "Legal-for-Trade Scale Calibration Compliance Router",
  "tags": [],
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "dbd3c9d6-2024-4566-b14e-5ab9b5979f78",
      "name": "__master_panel_0",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -336,
        -368
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 556,
        "height": 1119,
        "content": "\ud83d\udcd8 WORKFLOW DETAILS \u2014 Legal-for-Trade Scale Calibration Compliance Router\n\nVALUE PROP: Companies that own or service legal-for-trade scales (truck scales, grain scales, retail/deli scales) must have each device calibrated to NIST Handbook 44 tolerances and keep an auditable record of every pass/adjust/fail/condemn outcome for state weights-and-measures inspectors. This workflow takes a technician's field submission, computes the real tolerance math, has an AI classify the outcome using both the numbers and the technician's notes, and routes each device down a genuinely different compliance path.\n\nWHO / PROBLEM: Independent scale service companies and in-house weights-and-measures teams at grain elevators, truck terminals, and retail chains who currently fax or email calibration certificates and manage compliance cases in a shared spreadsheet with no automatic routing.\n\nEXECUTION WALKTHROUGH:\n1. Technician's mobile app POSTs a visit payload with one or more device readings to the webhook.\n2. Each device reading is split out individually.\n3. Code computes the %deviation between measured and test-load weight against a NIST HB44 tolerance band for the device's class.\n4. A data-quality gate catches malformed readings before they reach the classifier.\n5. A Text Classifier combines the numeric deviation with the technician's qualitative notes to choose exactly one of: compliant, out_of_tolerance_fail, condemned.\n6. A 3-way Switch sends each device down a different terminal path: compliant \u2192 certificate stored + state registry filed; out-of-tolerance \u2192 urgent owner alert + compliance case opened; condemned \u2192 state decommission notice + permanent record.\n7. All four possible terminal paths (including invalid submissions) are merged into one audit-log entry per visit.\n\nNODE SUMMARY: Webhook \u2192 Set \u2192 Split Out \u2192 Code \u2192 If \u2192 Text Classifier (+model) \u2192 Switch(3) \u2192 [Drive+HTTP | Gmail+Sheets | HTTP+Sheets] \u2192 Merge(4) \u2192 Aggregate \u2192 Sheets.\n\nEXPECTED INPUT: webhook POST {visit_id, technician, readings:[{device_id, site, device_class, test_load, measured_reading, technician_notes}]}.\nEXPECTED OUTPUT: a certificate in Drive and/or a state filing and/or an urgent Gmail alert and/or a decommission record, plus one consolidated audit-log row per visit.\n\nSTICKY COLOUR LEGEND: 1 blue=Trigger, 2 grey=Transform, 3 green=AI, 4 orange=Branch, 5 red=Storage, 6 yellow=Notify."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "698c32dd-0b38-45b3-b9be-d4440108f180",
      "name": "__master_panel_1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -336,
        816
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 6,
        "width": 556,
        "height": 657,
        "content": "\u2699\ufe0f SETUP GUIDE\n\n1. Import this JSON via n8n \u2192 Workflows \u2192 Import from File.\n2. Credentials required:\n   \u2022 Google Sheets OAuth2 \u2192 nodes \"Log Invalid Submission\", \"Log Compliance Case\", \"Log Decommission Record\", \"Append Consolidated Audit Log\" \u2014 placeholder: \"Google Sheets - Scale Calibration Registry\".\n   \u2022 OpenAI account \u2192 node \"Classifier Model\" \u2014 placeholder: \"OpenAI - Swapnil AI Labs Compliance\".\n   \u2022 Google Drive OAuth2 \u2192 node \"Store Certificate Of Conformance\" \u2014 placeholder: \"Google Drive - Calibration Certificates\".\n   \u2022 Gmail OAuth2 \u2192 node \"Send Urgent Out Of Tolerance Alert\" \u2014 placeholder: \"Gmail - Compliance Alerts\".\n   \u2022 HTTP Header Auth \u2192 nodes \"Submit Decommission Notice\", \"File State Registry Update\" \u2014 placeholder: \"State Weights & Measures Registry API Key\".\n3. Activate the Webhook node and give its production URL to your calibration app / field team.\n4. Replace the state registry URL with your actual state's weights-and-measures filing API (many states still require a portal upload \u2014 swap HTTP Request for a scheduled export if so).\n5. Update the Google Drive destination folder ID to your certificates folder.\nTEST: POST a sample payload with one in-tolerance and one grossly-out-of-tolerance reading and confirm both the Drive/HTTP path and the Gmail/Sheets path fire correctly.\nESTIMATED SETUP TIME: 35-45 minutes."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "6e07c696-6d9d-4b87-a111-4d821a9b2e59",
      "name": "__master_panel_2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -320,
        1536
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 3,
        "width": 540,
        "height": 426,
        "content": "\ud83c\udfa8 CUSTOMISATION\n\n1. In \"Compute Tolerance Deviation\" (Code), replace the simplified 3-class tolerance table with your state's full NIST HB44 acceptance/maintenance tolerance tables by capacity and division count.\n2. In \"Classify Compliance Status\" (Text Classifier), add a 4th category \"adjusted_in_field\" if your technicians can legally adjust and re-certify on the same visit.\n3. In \"Route By Compliance Status\" (Switch), add a 4th output for \"re-test-required\" devices that need a follow-up visit rather than an immediate pass/fail/condemn.\n4. In \"Send Urgent Out Of Tolerance Alert\" (Gmail), CC your state-mandated notification address if your jurisdiction requires immediate out-of-tolerance disclosure.\n5. Add a Split Out + Merge step after \"Append Consolidated Audit Log\" to also generate a PDF summary per visit for the customer."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "53a58b18-df84-448f-8ad9-ba43f8aa25b4",
      "name": "__master_panel_3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -336,
        2016
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 5,
        "width": 556,
        "height": 657,
        "content": "\u2139\ufe0f ADDITIONAL INFORMATION\n\nERROR HANDLING: Google Sheets, Google Drive, Gmail, HTTP Request and the Text Classifier are all set to continueRegularOutput with retryOnFail (3 tries, 2s backoff) so a single API hiccup does not lose a device's compliance outcome for the visit.\nAPI COST/RATE LIMITS: One OpenAI classification call per device reading (gpt-4.1-mini) \u2014 a 10-device visit costs a fraction of a cent. Google Drive/Sheets/Gmail are subject to normal Google Workspace API quotas; the state registry endpoint's rate limits are jurisdiction-specific.\nDATA PRIVACY: Device location/site data is commercial, not personal; the state registry submission is a public regulatory filing by design \u2014 confirm your jurisdiction's exact required fields before going live.\nBUILT AGAINST: n8n stable as of 2026-09-22. Node type strings confirmed against n8n-io/n8n-docs and n8n-io/n8n GitHub sources (including Switch v3 rules mode and Merge numberInputs); exact Text Classifier parameter internals are best-effort and should be spot-checked on first import.\nKNOWN LIMITATIONS: The tolerance table in Code is deliberately simplified for demonstration \u2014 a production deployment must encode the full NIST HB44 capacity/division tolerance tables. State registry API URL is a placeholder; most states do not yet expose a public filing API.\nCREATOR: Swapnil AI Labs \u2014 swapnil.mandloi7@gmail.com \u2014 swapnilailabs.netlify.app"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
